content.text:
Excellent — pathfinding works now (carrier reached site A at x=-13). But `game.bomb.plant is not a function` — the bot calls `game.bomb.plant(this)`, but BombController has `startPlant`, not `plant`. In botController: `game.bomb.plant(this)`. Also `game.bomb.planted` property doesn't exist — BombController has `state`; `!game.bomb.planted` is always truthy (undefined) — works by accident but sloppy. Fix bot to call startPlant and updatePlant like the player path.

Bot flow: when carrier in site, plantTimer += dt; after 1.6s → game.bomb.startPlant(this, true); then need to updatePlant until complete. Currently: startPlant sets state PLANTING; then bot's plant branch: `!game.bomb.planted` still true; plantTimer resets to 0 and continues; startPlant called again? `startPlant` checks `if (!this.canPlant(entity)) return false;` — canPlant returns false when state is PLANTING? canPlant: `if (this.state !== NOT_PLANTED && this.state !== PLANTING) return false;` — PLANTING allowed → startPlant re-calls... resets plantProgress each time! Infinite loop, never completes.

Proper fix in botController:
```js
if (this.team === 'attackers' && this.bombRole === 'carrier' && (game.bomb.state === 'notPlanted' || game.bomb.state === 'planting') && game.round.state === 'roundActive') {
  const site = this.map.siteAt(this.mesh.position);
  if (site && !this.target && !this.hasEnemyNear(game, 10)) {
    if (game.bomb.state === 'notPlanted') {
      if (game.bomb.startPlant(this, true)) this.plantTimer = 0;
    } else if (game.bomb.state === 'planting') {
      game.bomb.updatePlant(dt, true);
    }
    ...
```
Actually simpler: keep the timer for initiation, then while state==='planting', ensure bot stays (return null from objective? it's fine) and call updatePlant(dt, true) every frame. updatePlant checks plantingEntity alive + still in site → completes in 3.2s.

Rewrite the plant block:

```js
if (this.team === 'attackers' && this.bombRole === 'carrier' && game.round.state === 'roundActive') {
  const bombState = game.bomb.state;
  if (bombState === 'notPlanted' || bombState === 'planting') {
    const site = this.map.siteAt(this.mesh.position);
    if (site && !this.target && !this.hasEnemyNear(game, 10)) {
      if (bombState === 'notPlanted') {
        this.plantTimer += dt;
        this.mesh.setAction('plantBomb', 0);
        if (this.plantTimer > 1.2) { this.plantTimer = 0; game.bomb.startPlant(this, true); }
      } else {
        game.bomb.updatePlant(dt, true);
        this.mesh.setAction('plantBomb', 0);
      }
    } else if (this.plantTimer > 0) this.plantTimer = 0;
  }
}
```

Also while planting, attackObjective for carrier: `if (bomb.state === 'planted')...` — during 'planting' falls through to site logic: carrier inSite → hasEnemyNear false → return null → strafe. OK stays.

