Bomb went back to notPlanted — the plant aborted. Why? updatePlant in handleBomb: `if (this.bomb.state === PLANTING && this.bomb.isBotAction) this.bomb.updatePlant(dt, true)` — isBotAction true (I passed bot=true). updatePlant checks: `!stillHolding || !this.plantingEntity?.isAlive() || this.map.siteAt(this.plantingEntity.mesh.position)?.id !== this.site`. The player was teleported to (-18,0)... but the player update loop runs and map.resolveCollision — (-18,0) is inside site A, but is it inside a collider? Structure at (-18,7) no; (-20,-10) no. Hmm — but wait: `handleBomb` also processes the player branch: `if (player.team === 'attackers') { if (bombCanPlant(...)) { if (state NOT_PLANTED && input.interact) startPlant; if (state PLANTING) this.bomb.updatePlant(dt, input.interact); } }` — input.interact = false → updatePlant(dt, FALSE) → aborts the bot-driven plant! The player branch calls updatePlant with input.interact regardless of who initiated. That's the bug: player branch should only drive updatePlant when the plantingEntity is the player.

Fix in handleBomb:
```js
if (player.team === 'attackers') {
  if (bombCanPlant(this.bomb, player)) {
    if (this.bomb.state === BombState.NOT_PLANTED && input.interact) this.bomb.startPlant(player, false);
    if (this.bomb.state === BombState.PLANTING && this.bomb.plantingEntity === player) this.bomb.updatePlant(dt, input.interact);
  }
}
```
Same for defuse with defusingEntity === player.

